# Same values as the Vercel-deployed petrazim-trading-portal frontend,
# pointed at the same live Render backend so both UIs share one API/data.
VITE_API_URL=https://petrazim-trading-backend.onrender.com
VITE_WS_URL=wss://petrazim-trading-backend.onrender.com/ws

# Was missing entirely — root cause of both published sites (this one
# and the Lovable-published trade-hub, which mirrors this exact file)
# rendering as a blank page. integrations/supabase/client.ts calls
# createClient(SUPABASE_URL, ...) at module scope, and that module is
# reached through an EAGER import chain (main.tsx -> App.tsx ->
# FloatingTradeAI.tsx -> this client), not a lazy one, so it runs
# before ReactDOM.createRoot(...).render() — before AppErrorBoundary
# exists to catch anything. With VITE_SUPABASE_URL unset,
# @supabase/supabase-js throws "supabaseUrl is required." synchronously
# at that point, which aborts the whole module graph: the render call
# never happens, and the page is genuinely blank. Same reasoning as the
# VITE_API_URL/VITE_WS_URL entries above — Vite bakes every VITE_*
# variable into the public bundle at build time regardless of Vercel
# dashboard settings, and a Supabase publishable/anon key is designed
# to be public client-side (protected by Row Level Security, not
# secrecy) — so committing it here is the same pattern, not a new one.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://eacpktuyicxutatxuokw.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_CqcWu1zhFDKaFW7uBnIt1Q_tn3aU3xM